      "message": "fix(post): stop between setups by default (#1532)\n\nA two-setup document posted as one program ran from Setup 1's last cut\nstraight into Setup 2's first, on a part still clamped for Setup 1. A new\ndocument post option, Between setups, decides what posts at a setup\nchange: Pause (M0, the default), Optional stop (M1), Run straight on (the\nold program), or One file per setup.\n\n- The stop folds into the setup's last operation's after-action, with a\n  PARAM SetupChange naming the next setup; independent of \"Skip pauses\n  and homes\". A Go home at the change is refused by name.\n- Fanuc lifts Z (G91 G28 Z0) and writes (SETUP CHANGE - NEXT: <setup>)\n  before M0/M1; Tormach PathPilot now declares afterModes, lifts with\n  G53 G0 and shows (MSG, SETUP CHANGE - NEXT: <setup>). A post without\n  afterModes is refused at the change by name.\n- One file per setup splits the mounts per setup; the one-file post\n  refuses such a program by name.\n- Project key post_options.between_setups (written only off default),\n  setup-owned options compared for it, UI combo box, and the MCP post\n  tool's between_setups argument through the undoable SetPostOptions.\n\nFixes #1532\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
